  "helpTitle": "How to play together",
  "helpSectionRoomsTitle": "Playing with others",
  "helpSectionRoomsBody": "One person taps “Start a room” and picks a game. Klunki then shows a room code and a QR code.\n\nThe other person taps “Join a room” and scans the QR code or types the room code. Off you go.",
  "helpSectionWifiTitle": "On the same Wi-Fi",
  "helpSectionWifiBody": "Does one of you have the app? Then you need no server on the Wi-Fi: the app is the server itself, also for players in a browser (QR code).\n\nDevices on the same Wi-Fi find each other by themselves.",
  "helpSectionServerTitle": "When do you need a server?",
  "helpSectionServerBody": "Only if everyone plays in a browser or you are not on the same Wi-Fi. The server passes the moves between your devices.\n\nKlunki tells from the address what kind of server it is: “Server on the Wi-Fi” or “Server on the internet”.",
  "helpSectionOwnServerTitle": "Your own server on the Wi-Fi",
  "helpSectionOwnServerBody": "You can also run your own server on a computer on the Wi-Fi. A ready-made program for Mac, Windows and Linux is in preparation. You then enter its address in Klunki under “Advanced” with “change”.",
  "helpSectionComingTitle": "Easier soon (in preparation)",
  "helpSectionComingBody": "These ways to get a server are in preparation:\n• A server on the internet for a circle of friends (with Cloudflare, free)\n• A ready-made program to download for Mac, Windows and Linux\n• Docker for a NAS or Raspberry Pi\n\nServers on the internet are usually protected with a club code.",
  "helpSectionClubTitle": "What is a club code?",
  "helpSectionClubBody": "A club code is like a key to a server: only people who know it can start or join rooms there. You get it from the person who runs the server.\n\nKlunki only asks for it when a server needs one, and remembers it for that server.",
  "helpSectionDataTitle": "What happens to my data?",
  "helpSectionDataBody": "The server only passes the moves along and keeps none of them for good. If you play directly on the same Wi-Fi, nothing goes through someone else's server.\n\nThe club code stays on your device and never goes into room links or QR codes. You can see, change or remove it with “change” next to the server.",
